# Inactive identity compatibility facade

- `read_contract` and `checked` admit the complete proposed .12 contract and fixed72 normative sources. Contract-only checks require no actual current plan; supplied plans additionally require full G restoration.
- `identity_previous_*` returns .11. All nine source-next compatibility APIs preserve their signatures: `previous_*` returns .10 and `legacy_*` returns .8. Preparation returns nine descriptor dictionaries, including refreshed M06a2 dependencies and hash.
- Physical current inputs, fixed historical catalogue bytes and explicit callbacks have distinct origins. Admitted caller models are copied before external reads. Caller framing, historical overlap, remaining read allowances and private return copies are bounded; each context closes its raw caches before later phases. The64MiB logical limit is not a heap/RSS claim.
- A future thin loader must whole-pin actual D/G/C/capture/facade sources, including capture.py SHA9420ce4b9a73599b13c766c02a6f71f7f58199a70ff1c5ef0614f0e48b0c17da. This declaration does not perform that loader admission. Captured programs remain passive, and policy/catalogue defaults remain PENDING.
- Tests use explicitly staged799-unit data. No actual .12 loader, generator, contract, locks or seals are installed here. Actual generator-bound policy, reviewed source/proof lineage and real normative/generator/snapshot qualification remain required before atomic adoption; native/UI/backend restart and full SysON parity stay open.
